nodecode-shipframe is a rewrite of juanitourquiza's juanitourquiza/shipframe:

  https://github.com/juanitourquiza/shipframe
  commit 2d0a246206b7a3235c3167af5512d8dd4d8a29dd
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Juan Urquiza (LICENSE)

skills/ is that repository's skills/ folder, unchanged: 44 folders, a SKILL.md
in each, with the sibling files they name. Nothing converts them; Nodecode
reads a SKILL.md under a cell as a prose skill where it sits.

shipframe.lisp is ours. The upstream plugin registers its skills with a
dependency-free Python entrypoint; Nodecode's index reads the same folders
directly, so the entrypoint has no work left, and this one file takes its
place: the chain the skills walk, the pack by purpose, and the rules they
share, drawn from the repository's README at that commit. The installer for
Claude Code, Codex CLI and OpenCode (install.sh, hooks/, agents/, codex/,
opencode/, .claude-plugin/), the technology packs under project-packs/, the
templates, the wiki seed and the opt-in CI reviewer (scripts/) are left out:
they install into other harnesses or run in someone's CI, and none of them is
something a Nodecode cell can be.
